Revamp CMS — third-party data
==============================

Places (a registration form's Location field: "Noida, Uttar Pradesh, India")
  functions/lib/data/places.json is derived from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org):
  cities15000, the Indian places of cities1000, admin1CodesASCII and countryInfo
  (https://download.geonames.org/export/dump/). Place names, states and populations by GeoNames,
  licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Changes: the data was filtered (Indian places of
  1,000 people or more, other places of 15,000 or more or capitals; no historical, abandoned or
  destroyed places, and parts of cities only in India), reduced to name, state, country and population
  with a few alternative names for large cities, and written in a compact form by tools/build-places.js.
  The data is provided "as is" by GeoNames, without warranty.

Countries and dialling codes (a registration form's Mobile field)
  The country list and dialling codes in functions/lib/phone.js and templates/_shared/rv-forms.js are
  derived from GeoNames' countryInfo.txt (same licence as above); the number lengths follow the ITU-T
  E.164 national numbering plans as published by the ITU.

Time zones (which country a visitor's browser time zone is in)
  The time zone to country table in templates/_shared/rv-forms.js is derived from the IANA Time Zone
  Database (zone.tab and the links of tzdata.zi), which is in the public domain.
